1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,229
Every team at this hackathon has to submit a

2
00:00:04,229 --> 00:00:08,158
demo video. Most of us are making it right

3
00:00:08,158 --> 00:00:09,905
now, at 3 a.m.

4
00:00:09,905 --> 00:00:12,524
A good one needs a script,

5
00:00:12,524 --> 00:00:14,270
a clean recording, editing,

6
00:00:14,270 --> 00:00:16,017
a voiceover and captions.

7
00:00:16,017 --> 00:00:18,200
That's hours you don't have.

8
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:22,075
Pit Crew makes the pitch video for you.

9
00:00:22,075 --> 00:00:23,512
Paste your live link,

10
00:00:23,512 --> 00:00:25,309
or just your GitHub repo.

11
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:27,818
Here's a real run.

12
00:00:27,818 --> 00:00:29,335
I paste Excalidraw's link,

13
00:00:29,335 --> 00:00:33,130
pick a narrator, and ask to review the script first.

14
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:37,969
An agent on HarnessRouter explores the site and plans

15
00:00:37,969 --> 00:00:42,490
the pitch, while our server records each step in Chromium.

16
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:44,480
Before anything is voiced,

17
00:00:44,480 --> 00:00:47,039
I get the outline and a pitch check,

18
00:00:47,039 --> 00:00:48,959
and I can change any line.

19
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:53,801
Then it's voiced and rendered into a finished 1080p

20
00:00:53,801 --> 00:00:56,080
pitch video, ready to download.

21
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:10,756
No live link? OmniSTEM is just a GitHub repo.

22
00:01:10,756 --> 00:01:14,713
Pit Crew ran it inside a HarnessRouter sandbox and

23
00:01:14,713 --> 00:01:16,032
recorded it there.

24
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:23,826
DevPad's API ran the same way,

25
00:01:23,826 --> 00:01:27,355
and its video shows the real responses,

26
00:01:27,355 --> 00:01:28,868
sign-in errors included.

27
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:35,256
And Hunt the Wumpus,

28
00:01:35,256 --> 00:01:38,982
a Unity game, got its video from the team's

29
00:01:38,982 --> 00:01:43,536
own gameplay clip, narrated from frames the agent actually looked at.

30
00:01:48,300 --> 00:01:50,152
Here's how it works.

31
00:01:50,152 --> 00:01:54,320
Our server hands the project to an agent on

32
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:58,487
HarnessRouter, which explores the site or runs the repo

33
00:01:58,487 --> 00:02:02,655
in its sandbox, and writes the plan as JSON.

34
00:02:02,655 --> 00:02:06,822
Our server checks every statistic against its source page,

35
00:02:06,822 --> 00:02:10,064
records the demo, waits for your review,

36
00:02:10,064 --> 00:02:13,768
then ElevenLabs voices it and Remotion renders it.

37
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:17,985
Tonight we tested it on Excalidraw,

38
00:02:17,985 --> 00:02:20,638
Hoppscotch, Carbon, Mermaid and Squoosh,

39
00:02:20,638 --> 00:02:24,354
plus three student projects straight from GitHub.

40
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:29,059
Next: a pitch video for every launch.

41
00:02:29,059 --> 00:02:32,194
Product Hunt, demo days, investor updates.

42
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:36,277
Paste your link, and Pit Crew makes the pitch.
